>Many peoples I can think of have a seven-day week. At least the Bible-based=
> cultures seem to regard "sunday" as the last day of the 
>week (following the Biblical Genesis). As this "last" day is different to J=
>ews, Christians and Muslims, I'm wondering how this 
>influences the weekdays sequence respective.

I beg to differ. I don't know of any Christians who regard Sunday as the last
day of the week in Genesis, however they number the days today. If there are
any, they're ignorant. Greek, Spanish, and Portuguese distinguish the Lord's
day (Sunday) from the Sabbath (Saturday); Portuguese agrees with Greek that
Monday is the second day, though both are largely Christian.

