>I have no idea of the etymology underlying - maybe Ivan can help! But, agai=
>n: the counting begins with monday!

Szerda and csütörtök are obviously from Slavic. Péntek looks Greek, but it
disagrees with the Greek numbering, so it's probably Slavic too (Slavic had
nasal vowels, which are preserved in Polish, and the word for "five" had one).
Kedd may be from kettö, though I know little of Magyar so I'm just guessing.

